    "q-129255": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129255",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "Which statement is equivalent to $(¬P∨R)∧(¬P∨¬Q)?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we can factor out the disjunction with $¬P,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n(¬P∨R)∧(¬P∨¬Q)≡¬P∨(R∧¬Q)\n$$\n\nNow, since $R∧¬Q≡¬Q∧R,$ we can write\n\n$$\n¬P∨(R∧¬Q)≡¬P∨(¬Q∧R).\n$$",
